      CPU suspend saves gp at line 23 (REG_S gp, ...) and resume at __cpu_resume_enter:88 restores it via suspend_restore_regs macro (assembler.h:36-39). If an FDPIC process was running when the CPU suspended, gp is restored to the pre-suspend value without any FDPIC function-descriptor reload. Depends on the implicit invariant that the kernel never reschedules into a different FDPIC object after resume, or that FDPIC processes are not running during suspend. Very low probability trigger, but the pattern is structurally identical to the signal-path issue.
