      The C-level trap dispatcher orchestrates two actions that can change the execution target without updating gp: (1) sbi_trap_redirect at line 364, which rewrites regs->mepc to stvec and adjusts mstatus for S-mode delivery; (2) sbi_sse_process_pending_events at line 373, which may inject SSE events by rewriting regs->mepc to an SSE handler. Both modify mepc and mstatus in regs (which will be loaded by TRAP_RESTORE_MEPC_MSTATUS) but neither updates regs->gp. The assembly restore path will then blindly pop gp from regs at mret time. The trap_done ordering is also notable: SSE injection happens after trap redirection, so a redirected trap that also has a pending SSE event will first reload gp then potentially have SSE overwrite the execution target again.
  [RISK] lib/sbi/sbi_trap.c:103-232  sbi_trap_redirect
